# The build context is the repository root, because both Dockerfiles copy
# `backend/` and `frontend/` and `docker/nginx.conf` from there.
#
# node_modules matters most: a developer running compose locally has one built for
# their host platform, and COPY would carry it into a linux/amd64 image where the
# native parts do not load. The images install their own with `npm ci`.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
backend/data
**/.env
.env
*.log
